Package: NormGen
Title: An Efficient and Precise Quantile Mapping for Normal Pseudo-Random Number Generation
Version: 0.0.6
Authors@R: person("Piotr", "Sulewski", , "piotr.sulewski@upsl.edu.pl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: High-performance pseudo-normal random generator using an optimized 'quantile mapping' algorithm. It provides fast generation of normal pseudo-random numbers based on precise mathematical approximations. Version 0.0.5 updates the package and publication title to be more concise, precise, and readable for the community. Version 0.0.6- Added parallel_Rnorm(), a high-performance 'multithreaded' pseudo-normal random number generator powered by 'RcppParallel' and Intel 'TBB'. * Optimized package compilation flags to support multi-core parallel processing. Switched internal documentation and comments to English for full CRAN compliance.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), RcppParallel
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppParallel
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
License: GPL-3
Language: en-US
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
LazyData: true
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
